{
  "context": "1) Define and codify one runtime protocol for loader-resolved benchmarks.\n2) Extract shared result-construction logic into a single reusable module.\n3) Make both base classes delegate to that shared implementation, then close\n   remaining behavior gaps (minimal results, validation helpers).\n4) Migrate outlier benchmarks (nyctaxi, tsbs_devops) onto the canonical\n   runtime base contract with minimal behavior changes.\n5) Unify benchmark loader and benchmark registry metadata sources so supported\n   benchmark sets cannot drift.\n6) Add regression tests that assert contract conformance and lifecycle\n   behavior parity across representative benchmarks and modes.\n",
  "description": "BenchBox currently has a split benchmark runtime architecture:\n\n1) Most loader-resolved core benchmarks inherit `benchbox.base.BaseBenchmark`,\n   which contains a fallback result-building path.\n2) A smaller subset inherits `benchbox.core.base_benchmark.BaseBenchmark`,\n   which has newer lifecycle helpers and result-builder behavior.\n3) Some loader-resolved benchmarks (notably nyctaxi and tsbs_devops) inherit\n   neither base class and do not provide required runtime methods such as\n   `create_enhanced_benchmark_result`.\n\nThis divergence causes behavioral drift and latent regressions. A recent\nper-table timing fix landed in `benchbox.core.base_benchmark` but did not\npropagate to the dominant `benchbox.base` execution path used by most\nloader-resolved benchmarks.\n\nThis item unifies runtime behavior behind one canonical contract and one\nshared result-construction implementation, then migrates all loader-resolved\nbenchmarks to conform to that contract.",
  "legacy": {
    "anti_patterns": [
      {
        "dont": "patch only one base class path",
        "instead": "centralize behavior in one shared implementation",
        "item_id": "harmonize-benchmark-runtime-contract-and-base-classes",
        "why": "loader-resolved benchmarks use multiple inheritance paths"
      },
      {
        "dont": "silently change benchmark IDs, class names, or public CLI benchmark names",
        "instead": "preserve external identifiers and add explicit compatibility tests",
        "item_id": "harmonize-benchmark-runtime-contract-and-base-classes",
        "why": "that breaks user workflows and automation"
      },
      {
        "dont": "widen scope into unrelated platform adapter refactors",
        "instead": "constrain changes to benchmark base/loader/registry/runtime surfaces",
        "item_id": "harmonize-benchmark-runtime-contract-and-base-classes",
        "why": "this is a runtime-contract harmonization effort"
      }
    ],
